## Study overview

The study was conducted using a first-person driving simulator that combines SUMO traffic microsimulation with Unity 3D visualization. The experimental design compared driver responses to conventional yellow flashing lights and experimental blue flashing lights in a simulated freeway work zone on the MEX-015D toll freeway in Mexico.

A total of 51 licensed drivers participated in both experimental scenarios. The analysis focused on operating speed, acceleration, deceleration, and lane-changing maneuvers under controlled experimental conditions.

## Purpose of this repository

The purpose of this repository is to provide supplementary research materials supporting the study, including datasets, processing scripts, statistical results, survey information, and figures, to facilitate transparency and reproducibility of the reported analyses.

